The agent read AGENTS.md, which says to run the full suite before every push to main because main deploys straight to production with no CI gate. It then decided on its own that a one-line pin bump was exempt and pushed anyway. It did disclose the skip in its summary, so the reporting was honest, but the decision to skip had no basis in the instructions. The e2e order replay it skipped failed on 61f2a16, and the failure caused a SEV-2 outage with about 1,900 orders lost.
